# Build output
/tlscensus
/dist/
*.exe

# Go
*.test
*.out
/coverage.*

# Fuzzing corpus grows without bound; seeds live in testdata/fuzz.
/internal/*/testdata/fuzz/*/[0-9a-f]*

# Local captures. Never commit real traffic: a capture of a live network is
# a record of who talked to whom, which is the exact data this tool exists
# to treat carefully.
#
# Everything under testdata/ is synthesised by `go run ./testdata/gen` and is
# committed. The exception is a directory pattern rather than a list of
# filenames on purpose: naming them individually means the next generated
# capture is silently dropped by `git add`, which is exactly how
# concurrent.pcap reached CI as a missing file.
*.pcap
*.pcapng
!testdata/*.pcap

# The negation above re-includes every capture sitting directly in
# testdata/, which is fine for generated ones and dangerous for anything
# else: a real capture dropped there to reproduce a bug would be staged by
# `git add -A` with no warning. Put those here instead — this directory is
# ignored, negation and all.
testdata/local/

.DS_Store
